--- S0 gate, first run (AFTER repo_root=None fix, BEFORE UnsupportedProfileError fix) ---
.venv/bin/python scripts/s0_gate.py
  => receipt_cases=48 passed=48 (codex-norepo fixed by the repo_root=None
     change), determinism=100/100, BUT fail_closed=6/8:
     FC-02 production=INPUT_ERROR oracle=UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE,
     FC-03 production=INPUT_ERROR oracle=UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE.
     Root cause: the delegation wrapped the whole build_receipt_for
     call in try/except and folded UnsupportedProfileError into the
     (None, "production build_receipt failed: ...") pair, which the
     gate maps to INPUT_ERROR. The old code only wrapped build_receipt,
     so discovery errors propagated. Fixed by re-raising
     UnsupportedProfileError in build_production_receipt.
  (An earlier S0 run, before the repo_root=None fix, failed at the
   receipt index check on codex-norepo: production 3 sources / PASS
   vs oracle+expected 2 sources / BLOCK — build_receipt_for had
   auto-detected the enclosing P028 git repo as repo_root. Fixed by
   moving auto-detection to _run_receipt_command; repo_root=None now
   means no repo in the shared assembly function.)

